\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces The path of a bootstrapped gate. The two input ciphertexts are combined linearly; blind rotation computes the gate on the encrypted phase and gives a TRLWE ciphertext with fresh noise; sample extraction reads its constant coefficient as an LWE ciphertext under the key $s'$, of size $N$; and key switching brings it back to the key $s$, of size $n$, so that it can be used by the next gate. The dashed boxes are the two parts of the public evaluation key that the server has.}}{11}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:pipeline}{{6}{11}{The path of a bootstrapped gate. The two input ciphertexts are combined linearly; blind rotation computes the gate on the encrypted phase and gives a TRLWE ciphertext with fresh noise; sample extraction reads its constant coefficient as an LWE ciphertext under the key $s'$, of size $N$; and key switching brings it back to the key $s$, of size $n$, so that it can be used by the next gate. The dashed boxes are the two parts of the public evaluation key that the server has}{figure.6}{}}
