\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {12}{\ignorespaces Key switching for one coefficient $a_i$ of the extracted ciphertext. For each of the $t=8$ digit positions $j$, the table has an LWE encryption under $s$ of $v\cdot s'_i/4^j$ for every possible digit $v$. The base-4 digits of $a_i$ choose one entry per position; the chosen entries are subtracted from $(\mathbf  0,b)$, and zero digits are skipped. Doing this for all $N=1024$ coefficients replaces the part $\DOTSB \sum@ \slimits@ _ia_is'_i$ of the phase by the same value computed under the key $s$.}}{16}{figure.12}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:kstable}{{12}{16}{Key switching for one coefficient $a_i$ of the extracted ciphertext. For each of the $t=8$ digit positions $j$, the table has an LWE encryption under $s$ of $v\cdot s'_i/4^j$ for every possible digit $v$. The base-4 digits of $a_i$ choose one entry per position; the chosen entries are subtracted from $(\mathbf 0,b)$, and zero digits are skipped. Doing this for all $N=1024$ coefficients replaces the part $\sum _ia_is'_i$ of the phase by the same value computed under the key $s$}{figure.12}{}}
