\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {19}{\ignorespaces The offset trick for $t=0.7$, with $B_g=2^7$ and $\ell =3$. The offset has $64$ in each $7$-bit digit group and half of the last digit ($2^{10}$) in the part that is thrown away. After one 32-bit addition, each digit is obtained with a shift and a mask, and subtracting $64$ gives signed digits in $[-64,64)$. The ordinary digits of $t$ are $(89,76,102)$; the carries of the addition (red) make each digit that is $64$ or more negative and add $1$ to the digit on its left.}}{27}{figure.19}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:gadget}{{19}{27}{The offset trick for $t=0.7$, with $\Bg =2^7$ and $\ell =3$. The offset has $64$ in each $7$-bit digit group and half of the last digit ($2^{10}$) in the part that is thrown away. After one 32-bit addition, each digit is obtained with a shift and a mask, and subtracting $64$ gives signed digits in $[-64,64)$. The ordinary digits of $t$ are $(89,76,102)$; the carries of the addition (red) make each digit that is $64$ or more negative and add $1$ to the digit on its left}{figure.19}{}}
